(h) "Final destination" refers to the destination shown on the ticket presented at check-in, or, in the case of directly connecting flights, the destination of the last flight; alternative connecting flights are not considered unless the original scheduled arrival time is met.  
(i) "Person with reduced mobility" is a person whose mobility is limited due to a physical disability (such as sensory or locomotor impairment, permanent or temporary), intellectual disability, age, or other conditions requiring special attention and adaptation of available services to meet their needs.  
(j) "Denied boarding" refers to the refusal to allow a passenger to board a flight, despite meeting all boarding requirements set out in Article (3)(2), provided there are no valid grounds such as health, safety, security concerns, or inadequate travel documents.-;

